.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt PATINA-DISPLAYS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-displays
.Nd extend the desktop across several monitors, or mirror it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows a pill at the bottom of the primary screen, like the screenshot's,
naming the connected monitors and offering to
.Em Extend
the desktop across them, each showing its own part, to
.Em Mirror
it, each showing the same, or to leave it be.
The one in use is marked.
A monitor that is asked about stays off until it's chosen for, and the third tile,
.Em Do nothing ,
leaves it off; with no monitor waiting the third is
.Em Primary only ,
which turns the others off.
The compositor opens it on Ctrl+Super+P or the display key, the
.Ic displays
key in
.Ic [keys] ,
and when a monitor is plugged in that it has to ask about: one the desktop
hasn't seen, or one whose saved display has
.Dq Ask when plugged in
ticked in Settings.
A monitor it knows is switched on as the desktop was last used, without a
popup.
.Pp
A click or Enter chooses, the arrow keys and Tab move between the three, 1 to
3 choose, and Escape, or switching to another window, closes with nothing
changed.
Choosing extend with a monitor that has never been placed opens
.Xr patina-settings 1
at its Displays page, to say which side of another monitor it sits on.
.Pp
The choice is made through the compositor's
.Ql com.sectorflabs.Patina.Displays
on the session bus, so it only works under the Patina compositor on real
hardware.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin, by name.
.El
